  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0003] Raise BillingError with stable snake_case codes: Reject invalid input by raising ledgerly.errors.BillingError with a stable snake_case code as first argument (e.g. \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\", \"negative_amount\") and a repr/detail string as second.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0001] Round money only with round_money: Always round monetary values with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0002] Convert unit prices with to_money before arithmetic: Wrap raw unit prices with ledgerly.money.to_money before multiplying by quantity, and seed sums with the ZERO constant from ledgerly.money, as line_total and invoice_total do.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0004] Guard mutations on invoice.status == draft: Before mutating an invoice, check invoice.status != \"draft\" and raise BillingError(\"invalid_state\", ...) with the invoice id and status, matching issue_invoice.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
